## [2026-09-07T19:18:21+03:00] - Full-tree read: position after Muse steps 3-4 (code untouched)

Agent: Grok 4.6. Mandate: read the full project, report what it is, what is real vs claimed, and what to do immediately. No source/test/build edits this turn; only this append.

### How I looked

Tree + git (branch `engine` @ `5fc076e`, tracking `origin/engine` = `wayplot.git`) + `ORIGINAL_REQUEST.md` / `AGENTS.md` / `muse.ai` tail + subsystem manuals + every header/source under `include/` `src/` `tests/` + latest `logs/test_logs/` (not a fresh `make test` this session) + `tmp/dmabuf_present_probe.c` as the actual live composition. Cross-checked Muse claims against the code, not the other way around.

Host (observed): CachyOS `7.3.0-rc1-1-cachyos-rc`, i7-1165G7 (4c/8t), `WAYLAND_DISPLAY=wayland-0`, `/dev/dri/card0`+`renderD128`, `HugePages_Total=0` (THP/anon is the live hugepage path). Mesa prints Xe-experimental on every Vulkan test.

### What it is

A real dual-ring C23 Linux 7.2+ engine *library*: raw io_uring (no liburing), pure Wayland wire (no libwayland), Vulkan 1.4 dynamic rendering + Sync2 + BDA push constants (no WSI, no renderpass, no descriptor sets). ~15k lines of C/H/Slang. Tests: **93/93, 2005 assertions** in `logs/test_logs/test_20260907_190058.log` (~2.6 s native) and `sanitize_results.log` (~20.5 s ASan+UBSan).

The **product binary is still a topology smoke probe**. `engine_init()` brings Ring A/B up, MSG_RINGs `(uint64_t)topo.hugepage` (a host pointer, not a `VkDeviceAddress`), tears down. `make run` never connects to Wayland, never inits Vulkan, never presents. The live window lives in gitignored `tmp/dmabuf_present_probe.c`.

### Worktree vs HEAD

HEAD already has topology rework (cores 2/3, parked worker, pump, real offscreen frame). Uncommitted on top:

